WEBVTT

00:01.680 --> 00:06.330
It's gone! It's gone! 
I can't find it anywhere!

00:06.330 --> 00:08.110
What is it, Nikaidou?

00:08.690 --> 00:11.740
When I woke up, my false hand was missing!

00:14.010 --> 00:16.200
Somebody must've hidden it.

00:17.340 --> 00:19.220
'cause you always make so much noise with it.

00:19.860 --> 00:23.910
Shall I use my ueinkar to find it?

00:24.170 --> 00:26.420
Please do, Inkarmat-san!

00:31.340 --> 00:34.380
I feel a strong sensation coming 
from the direction of Koito Nispa.

00:37.910 --> 00:39.260
There it is!

00:39.930 --> 00:42.850
Amazing! How could you tell?

00:42.850 --> 00:43.940
It's such a mystery!

00:43.940 --> 00:46.270
Even I figured that one out.

00:46.510 --> 00:49.340
Inkarmat is amazing, Tsukishima!

00:50.640 --> 00:54.390
She answers any question 
you give her. It's scary.

00:54.390 --> 00:56.490
What are you biting?

00:56.940 --> 00:58.830
An ikema root, to ward off evil.

00:58.830 --> 01:01.110
It cost one yen and 20 sen.

01:01.110 --> 01:04.500
Hey, no stealing money from Lieutenant Koito.

01:05.210 --> 01:07.800
You don't believe me at all, do you?

01:07.800 --> 01:11.340
Fine, why don't you have 
her do her magic on you?

01:12.550 --> 01:14.090
I'll pass.

01:14.360 --> 01:17.560
Shall I see what I can see, Tsukishima Nispa?

01:17.890 --> 01:21.560
Is there anything you're seeking
 but unable to find?

01:26.690 --> 01:29.440
Don't think you can win me over.

01:32.000 --> 01:33.960
Am I right to think that 
Tanigaki Nispa can't come here,

01:33.960 --> 01:36.420
even though he must be back in Hokkaido,

01:36.890 --> 01:39.120
because I'm a hostage?

01:41.580 --> 01:44.120
Huh? The chopstick's not coming out!

01:44.120 --> 01:46.040
There's something inside?

01:47.830 --> 01:49.350
That's youkan.

02:28.980 --> 02:37.720
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

03:20.690 --> 03:25.510
<b>Episode Forty-Six
Perfect Mother</b>

03:28.780 --> 03:33.270
<i>I'm not the kind of cold-blooded 
man who could kill Sugimoto Saichi.</i>

03:35.270 --> 03:40.280
<i>Is it even possible to kill someone 
who can survive being shot in the head?</i>

03:41.130 --> 03:44.850
<i>Even if I kill him, Asirpa's not
 going to do as I say.</i>

03:45.560 --> 03:51.660
<i>No, Lieutenant Tsurumi would do whatever it 
took to get the information out of her.</i>

03:52.410 --> 03:55.920
<i>What I'm doing will bring misery to Asirpa.</i>

03:57.250 --> 04:00.750
<i>Would Huci be happy if I brought 
her granddaughter home as an empty,</i>

04:01.180 --> 04:03.370
<i>broken shell of herself?</i>

04:04.740 --> 04:10.990
<i>I could just pretend to search for her 
until the hunt for the gold is over.</i>

04:11.560 --> 04:13.550
<i>But it may take years...</i>

04:15.550 --> 04:19.730
<i>I wouldn't be able to see Inkarmat, 
or my newborn child, for that whole time...</i>

04:21.200 --> 04:24.980
<i>Does that mean my only choice is to find her?</i>

04:28.910 --> 04:30.760
It's been nine months, right?

04:30.760 --> 04:32.870
It could happen at any time.

04:33.480 --> 04:35.870
Those mysterious curves your body has now...

04:36.160 --> 04:39.210
Even if I ate you, I could 
never replicate them.

04:41.290 --> 04:45.470
Looking at you reminds me of my 
mother when she was pregnant.

04:46.170 --> 04:49.430
She was what I sought.

04:50.290 --> 04:54.110
In my mind, with her 
belly swollen, she was perfect.

04:54.660 --> 04:59.980
And I thought that she would be perfect, 
like Mother Mary, when she held her child.

05:00.460 --> 05:04.450
But she slipped on a staircase 
and had a miscarriage.

05:06.770 --> 05:10.410
I want to help you give birth to your child.

05:11.810 --> 05:13.500
That would make me very happy.

05:13.500 --> 05:16.040
I owe you my life.

05:16.040 --> 05:18.260
Give me the placenta, then!

05:18.260 --> 05:20.330
I've heard it's nutritious!

05:43.290 --> 05:45.810
I knew you'd come.

05:49.550 --> 05:52.090
<i>If I ask the people in the hospital</i>

05:52.550 --> 05:58.120
<i>where Inkarmat was moved, 
Tsurumi will find out I came here.</i>

05:59.040 --> 06:03.500
<i>I know I shouldn't try to look for her 
if it means putting her in danger.</i>

06:00.480 --> 06:09.760
<b><i>Shop
Nakagawa</i></b>

06:04.060 --> 06:09.760
<i>Am I just being selfish in 
wanting to take her away?</i>

06:10.750 --> 06:12.350
The perv's here.

06:14.730 --> 06:16.230
<i>Ikema root?</i>

06:17.980 --> 06:20.990
A perv with a big butt and big boobs,

06:20.990 --> 06:26.240
who looks like a hairy bear 
and lurks around the hospital.

06:27.650 --> 06:29.400
You're Tanigaki-san, right?

06:29.400 --> 06:35.040
My dad's in that hospital 
so I go in and out a lot.

06:35.590 --> 06:41.100
Inkarmat-san asked me to give 
this postcard to the pervy bear.

06:42.790 --> 06:45.050
<b>View of Otaru Port (Hokkaido)</b>

06:43.330 --> 06:44.360
This is...

06:45.050 --> 06:47.050
<b>View of Otaru Port (Hokkaido)</b>

06:47.660 --> 06:51.050
I failed to bring Asirpa back to Huci.

06:51.700 --> 06:55.060
I'm useless, which means I have to run.

06:55.500 --> 06:59.300
But I wanted to at least be with you and our child.

06:59.780 --> 07:01.190
Even if it put us all in danger.

07:01.190 --> 07:06.020
I left that postcard for you
hoping you'd come here.

07:06.340 --> 07:07.780
I'm ready for danger.

07:08.260 --> 07:10.530
Sergeant Tsukishima, your guard,
 went to the bath.

07:11.040 --> 07:13.530
He takes long baths, but hurry and get ready.

07:21.630 --> 07:22.540
Quiet!

07:26.090 --> 07:28.300
<i>The sound of a soldier's hobnailed boots!</i>

07:32.780 --> 07:33.850
From the second floor...

08:14.630 --> 08:20.600
If you're here, that means you've decided 
to disobey Lieutenant Tsurumi's orders, right?

08:21.020 --> 08:24.600
This was <i>your</i> choice, Private Tanigaki.

08:25.690 --> 08:27.730
Inkarmat, get off me!

08:28.170 --> 08:31.940
If this is your idea of justice, 
Tsukishima Nispa, then kill me first.

08:36.180 --> 08:36.990
Run.

09:03.100 --> 09:05.130
He won't be able to move for two hours.

09:05.560 --> 09:07.650
Get as far away from here as possible.

09:09.910 --> 09:15.610
You're wondering why a self-interested 
murderer like myself would do this?

09:16.420 --> 09:20.390
Inkarmat-san is about to become perfect.

09:21.140 --> 09:24.650
Please don't miss your chance 
to see that, Tanigaki-san.

09:25.890 --> 09:27.120
Ienaga-san...

09:28.600 --> 09:29.630
Let's go.

09:54.750 --> 09:55.490
Go.

10:05.040 --> 10:08.420
Why would Lieutenant Koito do that?

10:08.760 --> 10:14.170
Maybe he let us go because I told his 
fortune a lot when he was stuck in bed.

10:14.170 --> 10:16.720
That wouldn't be enough for him to do that...

10:17.060 --> 10:18.800
Not the Koito I know...

10:32.830 --> 10:34.780
Are you okay, Inkarmat?

10:34.780 --> 10:35.860
Are you cold?

10:37.670 --> 10:39.780
What's wrong? Does your stomach hurt?

10:40.360 --> 10:41.780
Being on horseback...

10:42.020 --> 10:44.070
I'm sorry, I was in too much of a hurry.

10:45.000 --> 10:47.060
We've made it out of town.

10:47.850 --> 10:49.750
Let's rest in that abandoned 
house for a while.

10:53.400 --> 10:55.760
Wait. I'll start a fire.

10:57.030 --> 10:59.610
Tanigaki Nispa, your head is bleeding.

11:04.490 --> 11:05.260
There we go.

11:05.990 --> 11:08.220
Let's rest a little more, then get going.

11:08.970 --> 11:10.480
We need to get away.

11:11.820 --> 11:13.480
Your leg is bleeding so badly.

11:13.480 --> 11:16.070
Those last two shots must've grazed me.

11:16.630 --> 11:18.240
I was so desperate to 
get away, I didn't notice.

11:22.860 --> 11:24.090
This is bad!

11:30.750 --> 11:32.750
Inkarmat, head out from the back!

11:32.750 --> 11:34.130
Hurry! Hurry!

12:01.200 --> 12:02.420
Tanigaki Nispa!

12:16.030 --> 12:18.000
Are you okay, Inkarmat?

12:18.250 --> 12:19.280
It's morning.

12:19.610 --> 12:22.760
But with my rifle he 
can't risk getting close.

12:23.230 --> 12:25.510
We can get away from him if 
we make it to the mountains.

12:25.510 --> 12:27.140
I know the mountains better than he does!

12:37.860 --> 12:40.020
What's wrong? Is he after us?

12:42.660 --> 12:44.360
I think my water broke.

12:49.130 --> 12:50.870
I'm sorry to do this after 
all you've done for us.

12:51.360 --> 12:52.320
Forgive me.

13:12.180 --> 13:14.900
So he made me chase the blood from his horse?

13:15.900 --> 13:17.640
Hang in there, Inkarmat!

13:17.640 --> 13:18.730
Hang in there!

13:19.440 --> 13:22.230
It's okay! I'm with you! You can do this!

13:22.500 --> 13:24.240
It'll all be fine!

13:46.960 --> 13:50.330
Huci... I'm sorry... I'm back.

13:51.070 --> 13:55.980
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

14:01.610 --> 14:05.190
There's someone from the 7th 
watching this village, right?

14:05.240 --> 14:07.280
<b>Osoma's Mother</b>

14:05.720 --> 14:07.280
Don't worry.

14:07.650 --> 14:11.730
Every night, my husband gets him drunk.

14:11.730 --> 14:15.810
Even if Osoma steps on 
his face, he won't wake up!

14:21.160 --> 14:22.290
What's Huci doing?

14:22.530 --> 14:25.420
She's touching to see if it's a boy or girl.

14:25.650 --> 14:28.320
It's said that if it's a boy, 
you must deliver it face-down,

14:28.320 --> 14:32.680
and a girl it must be face-up, 
or they won't live a long life.

14:32.960 --> 14:35.910
You can tell which it is 
by touching their stomach?

14:35.910 --> 14:38.560
Supposedly the size of 
the hip bones tells you.

14:38.780 --> 14:40.770
Only a very few can do it, even then.

14:41.340 --> 14:44.900
She says that her personal god, 
who dwells just behind her neck, tells her.

14:45.590 --> 14:48.760
Huci has been helping women 
give birth since she was 19.

14:48.760 --> 14:53.450
She's a veteran ikoinkarmat, or midwife.

14:53.700 --> 14:56.700
She helped give birth to Asirpa, too.

14:57.070 --> 15:00.170
Okay, I'll leave her to you.

15:00.880 --> 15:04.170
Sergeant Tsukishima knows about this kotan.

15:04.170 --> 15:07.050
He'll realize we're here and come after us.

15:07.700 --> 15:08.760
I'll fight him in the mountains.

15:08.980 --> 15:10.810
No, Tanigaki Nispa.

15:10.810 --> 15:12.170
Don't fight him.

15:12.170 --> 15:14.740
I'll come back. I'm immortal.

15:15.750 --> 15:18.430
You're not immortal. Run!

15:25.220 --> 15:26.070
What?!

15:26.070 --> 15:27.230
Stop!

15:30.630 --> 15:34.530
Just kill me! Don't hurt 
Inkarmat or the others!

15:34.780 --> 15:40.210
Private Tanigaki, you started making 
the wrong choice a long time ago.

15:40.720 --> 15:44.360
When you met her and the old woman 
instead of coming back to the unit.

15:45.990 --> 15:47.250
Tsukishima!

15:48.170 --> 15:49.470
Enough, Tsukishima!

15:49.470 --> 15:50.510
Stop it!

15:50.760 --> 15:55.430
Were you following me to 
see if they could get away?

15:56.280 --> 15:58.740
What's the point of killing the two of them?

15:59.200 --> 16:03.660
We have other ways to find Asirpa 
besides relying on Tanigaki!

16:04.050 --> 16:06.060
If someone wants to run, let them!

16:06.320 --> 16:09.440
You need to follow through on 
a threat or it's worthless.

16:09.440 --> 16:11.530
The others might start getting ideas.

16:12.840 --> 16:15.400
I told you I'd kill you if you interfered.

16:16.230 --> 16:19.490
Does this mean you're 
betraying Lieutenant Tsurumi, too?

16:20.530 --> 16:23.080
Which are you, Lieutenant Koito?

16:23.950 --> 16:28.690
Are you one of the traitors, suspicious 
that Lieutenant Tsurumi used both

16:28.690 --> 16:30.210
you and your father?

16:32.430 --> 16:33.730
Put your gun down.

16:33.730 --> 16:35.450
That's an order as your superior officer.

16:35.970 --> 16:39.240
I'm prepared to watch 
both you and Lieutenant Tsurumi

16:39.240 --> 16:41.310
with my own eyes until the end of all this.

16:43.170 --> 16:48.880
Tsukishima, you said that the people 
who follow Lieutenant Tsurumi will be saved,

16:48.880 --> 16:52.280
and that you saw nothing wrong with that.

16:52.760 --> 16:54.290
I agree.

16:54.810 --> 16:59.330
Even if both my father and I were 
used for that purpose, I don't care.

17:01.480 --> 17:06.860
But if Lieutenant Tsurumi has a 
true goal, then I want to see what it is!

17:07.540 --> 17:11.210
If there's no justice at the end of 
it that I can be satisfied with...

17:12.140 --> 17:14.920
The guilt and regret will kill me.

17:15.690 --> 17:19.640
And that's why we can't kill those two!

17:19.850 --> 17:21.470
It's too late for me!

17:22.160 --> 17:23.750
I've killed so many people!

17:24.130 --> 17:26.480
I've used them and sent them to their deaths!

17:26.480 --> 17:27.940
It's not too late!

17:29.210 --> 17:31.990
I've given up on what was truly important...

17:33.710 --> 17:35.070
and thrown it away.

17:36.560 --> 17:39.450
All I have left is doing my job.

17:40.700 --> 17:46.160
Does that sternness come from bearing the 
weight of what you threw away, Tsukishima?!

17:54.990 --> 17:55.920
Inkarmat...

18:01.630 --> 18:02.600
She was...

18:10.060 --> 18:11.080
Inkarmat!

18:12.810 --> 18:15.280
The baby's about to come out! Everyone help!

18:15.800 --> 18:17.990
You go heat up a lot of water!

18:18.330 --> 18:21.070
You go gather up a bunch 
of straw from nearby!

18:21.280 --> 18:23.160
And you watch him!

18:27.360 --> 18:28.160
You three!

18:29.010 --> 18:31.130
Go get these from the other houses.

18:31.510 --> 18:32.560
Noyaham.

18:32.560 --> 18:34.590
Gauze made from sagebrush.

18:34.590 --> 18:36.510
It's better for stopping 
bleeding than cotton.

18:37.050 --> 18:39.160
Put the rasupakap in the hot water.

18:39.160 --> 18:43.430
That creates a disinfectant 
that helps lubricate the birth canal.

18:43.800 --> 18:46.430
Hang this tar strap from the beam above!

18:46.430 --> 18:48.180
She'll pull on it to brace herself!

18:48.720 --> 18:52.420
Put the straw on the left side of the 
fireplace and put some old rags on it.

18:52.420 --> 18:53.920
That's where she'll give birth!

18:57.370 --> 19:04.610
Uwarikamuy pirka no enteksama, 
epunkine yakun pirka nuwap.

19:04.610 --> 19:11.850
Hapurnuwap kiwa kamuy kirsam 
eponpesanke kusunena.

19:15.270 --> 19:17.240
Get inside!

19:18.250 --> 19:20.130
Carry the mortars to the 
entrance of the house!

19:21.290 --> 19:22.640
Nisu horipire.

19:23.300 --> 19:26.190
It's a ritual we do for difficult births, 
called "making the mortar dance"!

19:26.190 --> 19:29.100
Roll it harder! Harder!

19:29.510 --> 19:32.350
<i>Huci put gauze beneath the sole of her foot</i>

19:32.660 --> 19:34.910
<i>and pressed it against the 
pregnant woman's anus.</i>

19:34.910 --> 19:43.110
<i>The Ainu rotate the baby during birth depending
 on its sex, a technique called kemakokiru.</i>

20:14.610 --> 20:17.360
You did great, Inkarmat.

20:18.000 --> 20:21.130
Hold the baby in your arms, Tanigaki Nispa.

20:25.970 --> 20:27.450
He's got a huge dick!

20:27.450 --> 20:29.870
That's what's left of the umbilical cord.

20:31.930 --> 20:34.330
So I've got a daughter...?

20:36.050 --> 20:36.790
Hey, wake up.

20:41.510 --> 20:44.260
I'll keep this a secret from Lieutenant Tsurumi.

20:44.260 --> 20:47.380
Spend a week in town to cool your head.

20:47.840 --> 20:51.550
And then continue to report to him 
that nothing unusual has happened.

20:53.000 --> 20:56.100
Thank you, Lieutenant Koito!

21:00.730 --> 21:02.340
Tanigaki Nispa!

21:02.650 --> 21:05.070
Osoma... How've you been?

21:05.320 --> 21:06.820
Osoma!

21:14.640 --> 21:16.000
Lieutenant Koito...

21:16.640 --> 21:19.000
Did you really mean that?

21:19.590 --> 21:22.340
Or were you simply trying to 
convince me to put down the gun?

21:23.500 --> 21:25.340
Whichever you prefer.

21:26.490 --> 21:27.960
But it just seems to me that

21:27.960 --> 21:32.370
Lieutenant Tsurumi isn't the kind of man whose
 goal is something as petty as lust for power,

21:33.090 --> 21:39.730
or a desire to sacrifice everyone 
else to enrich himself.

21:41.050 --> 21:45.740
Do you have no idea what 
his real objective is?

21:46.960 --> 21:50.550
He may not have one.

21:51.050 --> 21:56.410
He may truly want to properly bury his 
comrades and ensure prosperity for Japan.

22:03.580 --> 22:05.260
Finger bones...

22:05.930 --> 22:08.010
Have you ever seen those finger bones?

22:08.560 --> 22:10.010
Whose finger bones?

22:11.260 --> 22:14.140
Never mind. It might not be relevant.

22:16.760 --> 22:21.700
Fighting and dying for his comrades is 
the most noble thing a soldier can do.

22:22.460 --> 22:23.730
Right, Tsukishima?

22:24.780 --> 22:28.650
Your stance toward 
Lieutenant Tsurumi isn't healthy.

22:29.150 --> 22:32.010
I'm going to believe in the best in him.

22:32.370 --> 22:34.950
So you believe in me and follow me!

22:42.030 --> 22:43.740
This is what I mean, Tsukishima!

22:43.740 --> 22:45.330
I don't understand.

22:45.880 --> 22:49.760
<b>One Week Later</b>

22:50.410 --> 22:53.610
I'll tell them you two escaped.

22:54.200 --> 22:57.230
Head south so that you 
don't run into the others.

22:57.550 --> 23:00.960
Thank you, Koito Nispa.

23:00.960 --> 23:03.290
I wish the three of you the best.

23:04.220 --> 23:05.530
Tsukishima Nispa...

23:06.460 --> 23:09.990
I did see something with my clairvoyance...

23:11.610 --> 23:12.930
I don't need to hear it.

23:26.030 --> 23:29.560
<i>Huci saved me again... I'm always 
the one who gets saved.</i>

23:35.240 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Steamship</b>

23:35.750 --> 23:38.710
Next time: "Steamship"!
